// Nucleo-H743ZI with CAN, for SIL execution under Renode.
//
// Renode 1.16.1 ships no `platforms/boards/nucleo_h743zi.repl`. It ships
// `platforms/cpus/stm32h743.repl` (the die) and `platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl`
// (the same Nucleo-144 carrier around the H753 die). This file is the missing
// combination: the stock H743 CPU description plus the Nucleo-144 board wiring,
// taken from the stock H753 board file.
//
// The `using` path is resolved against the Renode installation root, so this
// inherits the stock CPU description rather than forking a copy of it. Renode
// upgrades therefore surface here as a diff to review, not as silent drift.
//
// What the stock CPU file already provides, and why we do not redeclare it:
//
//   flashBank1  0x08000000  1 MiB   - where the ELF lands
//   flashBank2  0x08100000  1 MiB
//   itcm        0x00000000  64 KiB
//   dtcm        0x20000000  128 KiB
//   axiSram     0x24000000  512 KiB - Zephyr's main SRAM for this board
//   sram1..4, backupSram
//   usart3      0x40004800          - Zephyr's console for nucleo_h743zi
//                                     (ST-Link virtual COM port)
//   fdcan1      0x4000A000  CAN.MCAN, Line0 -> nvic@19, Line1 -> nvic@21
//   fdcan2      0x4000A400  CAN.MCAN
//   canMessageRAM 0x4000AC00 +0x2800 - shared message RAM for both FDCAN cores
//
// NOTE ON PERIPHERAL NAMING: the CAN controller is `fdcan1`, not `can0`. The
// harness refers to it as `sysbus.fdcan1`. Peripheral names here must match the
// emulator's actual names, never a tidier invention -- a name that does not
// resolve is a run that cannot happen.

using "platforms/cpus/stm32h743.repl"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Nucleo-144 carrier board. Same layout as the stock nucleo_h753zi.repl.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GreenLED: Miscellaneous.LED @ gpioPortB 0

YellowLED: Miscellaneous.LED @ gpioPortE 1

RedLED: Miscellaneous.LED @ gpioPortB 14

UserButton1: Miscellaneous.Button @ gpioPortC 13
    -> gpioPortC@13

gpioPortB:
    0 -> GreenLED@0
    14 -> RedLED@0

gpioPortE:
    1 -> YellowLED@0

// The Nucleo-144 carries an LAN8742A PHY on RMII. Zephyr's networking stack is
// not enabled in the BMS build, but the PHY is modelled so that a board without
// it does not read as a board that has one.
phy: Network.EthernetPhysicalLayer @ ethernet 0
    BasicControl: 0x3100
    BasicStatus: 0x782D
    Id1: 0x0007
    Id2: 0xC130
    AutoNegotiationAdvertisement: 0x01E1
    AutoNegotiationLinkPartnerBasePageAbility: 0x0001
    AutoNegotiationExpansion: 0x0064
    AutoNegotiationNextPageTransmit: 0x2001
